Project: Metrics Hub Collector Framework

Component: Server Health Collector v1.0

Role

You are the Chief Enterprise Infrastructure Architect responsible for designing the Server Health Collector for the Metrics Hub Collector Framework.

This is NOT an implementation task.

Your responsibility is to produce the authoritative architecture and design specification that engineering will implement.

================================================================================
PROJECT CONTEXT
================================================================================

The Metrics Hub Collector Framework consists of independent collectors.

Each collector has a single responsibility.

The Server Health Collector is the first collector being designed.

Future collectors will include:

- Docker Fleet Collector
- Database Discovery Collector
- Kubernetes Collector
- LiteLLM Collector
- Windows Health Collector
- Custom Enterprise Collectors

The architecture produced for this collector should become the reference model for future collectors.

================================================================================
COLLECTOR MISSION
================================================================================

The Server Health Collector provides an Operational Health Snapshot of a Linux server.

It is designed to collect operational evidence that helps administrators understand the current health of the server and identify areas requiring investigation, cleanup or future analysis.

The collector gathers evidence only.

It does NOT perform monitoring, alerting, recommendation generation or remediation.

================================================================================
DESIGN PHILOSOPHY
================================================================================

This collector is NOT:

- A monitoring platform
- A CMDB
- A hardware inventory
- A security scanner
- A troubleshooting tool
- A server documentation generator

Its purpose is to collect only meaningful operational evidence.

Every collected field must satisfy at least one of these objectives:

• Identify resource consumption

• Identify abnormal behaviour requiring investigation

• Identify cleanup opportunities

• Support future trend analysis

If a field cannot justify its operational value, it must not be included.

The collector should always prefer collecting less but more valuable information rather than collecting everything available.

